SOAPBOX: Operated unassisted for most of the contest after a plethora
SOAPBOX: of incoming spots at the beginning of the contest significantly
SOAPBOX: slowed the computer and keying. Conditions were fine and allowed
SOAPBOX: for a few good runs. On Saturday night, 40 and 80 were very
SOAPBOX: noisy, so I decided to go to 20, working lots of RA. After
SOAPBOX: missing my alarm on Sunday morning, I hopped on 20 for most of
SOAPBOX: the day while also occasionally switching to 15 and 10 to work
SOAPBOX: mults. On Sunday evening, I finally decided to connect to the
SOAPBOX: cluster, allowing me to work many mults. With three or four hours
SOAPBOX: remaining in the contest, I dropped to 40 a bit earlier than I
SOAPBOX: normally would have. This allowed me to claim a nice run
SOAPBOX: frequency that I ran on with decent rate until the end. Overall,
SOAPBOX: a fun semi-serious effort. Thank you to Jim, K1IR, for the use
SOAPBOX: of his station.
